// DEMO 3 of 5 - THE LAST TRAIN.  Every READY card in studio/motions/, used as filmmaking.
//
//   python3 studio/compile.py studio/movies/demo_motion.movie --timeline
//   python3 scripts/short.py studio/movies/demo_motion.json
//
// WHAT THIS ONE IS FOR, AND HOW IT DIFFERS FROM motion-proof.movie
//
// motion-proof.movie walks the four RUNGS of compose.resolve_motion() - card, free text,
// derived, hold - one beat each, to prove the resolver works. This one walks the LIBRARY.
// studio/motions/ holds 34 cards and exactly nine are marked `ready`; all nine are here,
// each on a shot template ITS OWN CARD names in its `shots` field, inside a piece that
// plays as a film rather than as a test grid:
//
//   hold_frame        establish   the empty platform      (stillness, chosen on purpose)
//   papers            insert      the litter on the floor (element)
//   walk_in           build       she arrives             (subject, 1girl)
//   cup_lift          speak       she waits               (subject, staged in reach)
//   hand_to_face      speak       she answers him         (subject)
//   walk_in_only      master      he boards               (subject, 1boy - REGENDER)
//   hand_to_face_only react       he cannot say it        (subject, 1boy - REGENDER)
//   turn_away         master      she gives up the face   (subject, and it costs the face)
//   confetti          establish   the carriage leaves     (element the keyframe lacks)
//
// Four more beats DERIVE from their shot lines, so the film also shows the rung that costs
// nothing to author: a ticket dropping through the gap, a hand reaching toward the window,
// steam pouring from under a locomotive, a door sliding shut across the frame.
//
// THE REGENDER PATH IS THE POINT OF HAVING TWO CHARACTERS. Every card in the library is
// written in the third person feminine, because that is how the probe cells that measured
// them were written - "She walks forward toward the camera." NIKA is 1girl and takes the
// card verbatim. VIRO is 1boy and compose._motion_regender() must rewrite the same card to
// "He walks forward toward the camera." before it reaches LTX, because a keyframe drawn as
// a man plus a motion string asking for a woman is a contradiction the video model
// resolves by changing somebody's face.
//
// NOT ONE BEAT IN THIS FILM FALLS TO THE UNINTENDED HOLD. The one beat that does hold -
// the opening establish - holds because hold_frame was NAMED, and hold_frame rather than
// hold_nobody: 'Nobody moves.' was rendered over a keyframe written 'no humans' and by
// frame 24 the model had walked a figure into shot and marched it away down the corridor.
// The model renders nouns and 'Nobody' is a person-shaped one. hold_frame names no
// occupant at all.
//
// TWO CARDS IN ONE SCENE, which nothing in this project had done. A per-shot @token beats
// the scene's, so `motion: hand_to_face` on the scene and `@cup_lift` on the shot line
// gives the picture beat one card and the descless dialogue beat that follows it another -
// and that dialogue beat is the beat class that holds in every earlier film.
//
// cup_lift IS STAGED. Its re-measurement across four stagings found the precondition is
// not "a cup in frame" but "a cup WITHIN REACH": at arm's length the full look-reach-lift-
// drink lands; a table's length away the card turns into the subject walking out of frame
// while still returning a healthy-looking number. So the mug is written into her hands.
//
// look: moonlit and sodium, never `night`. studio/looks/night.json grades
// brightness=-0.15 with contrast=1.20 and that arithmetic drives everything under luma 60
// to pure black on this box - a station platform at night would come back as a rectangle.

MOVIE demo_motion
  title: DEMO MOTION
  logline: She is on the platform to leave and he is on the train to stay, and neither of them says so.
  canvas: 1920x1080
  fps: 24
  engine: anime
  style: ova_80s
  checkpoint: animagine-xl-4.0.safetensors
  face_weight: 0.6
  seed_root: demo-motion-1
  clip_secs: 5
  tags: cinematic

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CHAPTER the_platform
  look: moonlit
  place: subway_platform
  pace: normal
  // NOT lonely_night_city, WHICH CANNOT RENDER. studio/cues/lonely_night_city.json
  // carries key "B flat minor" and ComfyUI TextEncodeAceStepAudio1.5 accepts a fixed
  // 34-value list that spells it "Bb minor". The graph fails validation, short.py
  // aborts - AFTER every keyframe and every clip has been generated, which is the most
  // expensive place in the pipeline to discover it. heroic_fanfare (B flat major) and
  // menace (E flat minor) are broken the same way; the other 19 cues are fine.
  cue: unease

  // hold_frame, NAMED. The correct answer for this beat is stillness and the film says so
  // out loud rather than arriving at it by failing to derive anything.
  SCENE empty_platform
    transition: fade_black
    camera: static
    shot: establish @hold_frame | an empty underground platform at night, tiled walls, one lit sign, wet concrete, no humans, wide shot

  // rung 3: nothing is named, the shot line does the work.
  SCENE the_ticket
    transition: cut
    place: the edge of a station platform, yellow line, a dark track bed below, litter
    camera: static
    shot: insert | a paper ticket dropping through the gap onto the tracks, no humans, close-up

  SCENE she_arrives
    transition: dissolve
    characters: NIKA
    emotion: resolve
    camera: static
    shot: build @walk_in | coming up the platform toward the camera, canvas bag over one shoulder, full body

  // TWO CARDS, ONE SCENE. @cup_lift on the picture beat, hand_to_face on the scene so the
  // line of dialogue underneath it moves as well.
  SCENE she_waits
    transition: cut
    characters: NIKA
    emotion: longing
    motion: hand_to_face
    mood: an enamel mug held in both hands at chest height, steam, tiled wall behind
    camera: static
    shot: speak @cup_lift | seated on a platform bench with a mug in both hands at chest height, close-up
    NIKA: The four twenty is the last one. After that it is the morning.

  SCENE the_papers
    transition: cut
    place: wet concrete platform floor, yellow safety line, loose sheets of newspaper lying on the concrete
    camera: static
    shot: insert @papers | loose newspaper lying across a wet concrete floor, no humans, close-up

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CHAPTER the_carriage
  look: sodium
  place: train_carriage
  pace: normal
  cue: melancholy_piano

  // REGENDER: walk_in_only is written "She walks forward toward the camera." and VIRO is
  // 1boy. This beat is the one that must come back masculine.
  SCENE he_boards
    transition: dissolve
    characters: VIRO
    emotion: doubt
    camera: static
    shot: master @walk_in_only | walking up the aisle of a lit carriage toward the camera, full body

  // rung 3 again, on a person this time: the shot line names a mover, a verb and a path.
  SCENE the_window
    transition: cut
    characters: NIKA
    emotion: longing
    camera: static
    shot: react | reaching one hand toward the carriage window, close-up

  SCENE he_cannot_say_it
    transition: cut
    characters: VIRO
    emotion: resignation
    motion: He leans back against the seat away from the window.
    mood: half his face in sodium light from the window, medium close-up
    camera: static
    shot: react @hand_to_face_only | seated by the window with one hand rising toward his face, close-up
    VIRO: You should get on. I am not going to ask you to.

  SCENE she_answers
    transition: cut
    characters: NIKA
    emotion: angry
    motion: She takes one step back from the carriage door into the dark.
    mood: standing in the carriage doorway, one hand on the frame, medium shot
    camera: static
    shot: speak @hand_to_face | standing in the carriage doorway, close-up
    NIKA: You never ask. That has always been the whole of it.

  SCENE the_steam
    transition: cut
    place: the underside of a stopped locomotive on a wet platform, iron wheels, gravel
    camera: static
    shot: insert | steam pouring from under a stopped locomotive, no humans, close-up

  // turn_away DELIBERATELY GIVES UP THE FACE. Measured: identity holds about 8s but budget
  // by the ACTION - on a turn the face is frontal to 5s, profile at 7s and back-of-head by
  // 8s. clip_secs is 5 on this beat for exactly that reason.
  SCENE she_turns
    transition: cut
    characters: NIKA
    emotion: resignation
    camera: static
    shot: master @turn_away @5s | standing in the open carriage door, medium shot

  // confetti is ABSENT from the keyframe and the model invents it - the highest-motion
  // card in the library at mean 6.127, and the one seed in three that measured 10.15 will
  // bury the frame. It is the last shot of the film, which is where that risk is cheapest.
  SCENE the_carriage_leaves
    transition: fade_black
    silence: true
    camera: static
    shot: establish @confetti | an empty lit train carriage seen from a dark platform, doors open, no humans, wide shot
